Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:15:17 +0000
Subject: effect colour

Set a new effect record's colour before its first draw.

The record is drawn once with what the stack held before func_002ED368 sets its colour and
alpha (+0x30, +0x38). Retail's stack held 0x001A0000 and 0x001C0000 there at every spawn of a
New Game flight, an alpha byte of 0, so that draw changes no pixel; the port's stack held float
bits. The values retail had are set now.
---
 src/game/002E76C0-g8.c     | 6 ++++++
 src/game/002E7BC8-g8.c     | 6 ++++++
 src/pal/game/002E84A8-g8.c | 6 ++++++
 src/pal/game/002E89D0-g8.c | 6 ++++++
 4 files changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/game/002E76C0-g8.c b/src/game/002E76C0-g8.c
index 46576b4..a0c512a 100644
--- a/src/game/002E76C0-g8.c
+++ b/src/game/002E76C0-g8.c
@@ -36,6 +36,12 @@ void func_002E76C0(void *object, int index, int alternate)
  float *entry;
  int count1, count2, low, high;
  unsigned int color1, color2;
+ /* OpenRAC: the new record's colour and alpha now (+0x30, +0x38) are never set here: it is drawn once
+    with what the stack held, before func_002ED368 sets them. Retail's stack held 0x001A0000 and 0x001C0000
+    there at every spawn of a New Game flight, an alpha byte of 0, so that draw changes no pixel; the host's
+    held float bits, a puff of alpha up to 0xFD at the engine every tick. */
+ effect.unknown = 0x001A0000;
+ effect.unknown2 = 0x001C0000;
  next = *(unsigned long long *)(*(char **)(o + 0x5c) + 0x10);
  func_00283130(first, *(unsigned long long *)(*(char **)(o + 0x58) + 0x10));
  func_00283130(second, next);
